# The Test Cabinet — web console DEV defaults (`@clockwyrks/web`).
#
# Vite loads `.env.development` ONLY in development mode — i.e. for
# `npm run -w apps/web dev` (`vite --host`), never for `vite build` (production
# mode), so nothing here is baked into the shipped tcab-web image.
#
# The local service stack (backend, artifacts, arena) runs on the k3d cluster —
# NOT the web console, which you run from source with this dev server. The dev
# server proxies `/api`, `/artifacts` and `/arena` to the addresses
# `make -C deployments/local local-forward` exposes on localhost (see
# vite.config.ts), adding the local identity header the services attribute every
# request to. The console names no service URL: it addresses the backend at
# `/api` of its own origin, which is that proxy here and the edge in a
# deployment, so every request carries the identity.
#
# To override (e.g. aim the proxy elsewhere), set TCAB_PROXY_BACKEND,
# TCAB_PROXY_ARTIFACTS, TCAB_PROXY_ARENA or TCAB_PROXY_IDENTITY in a gitignored
# `.env.development.local`, which Vite loads with higher precedence.
